// Yarn Spinner — Instructor Tai follow-up dialogue (after act1_aen_of_lantern_heights cutscene)
// Speaker: Instructor Tai, Lantern Heights dojo master
// Voice: calm, direct, speaks to Aen as someone who already belongs here — not a tourist
title: greeting
tags: root
---
Instructor Tai: You know this place already, Aen. You don't need me to explain the walls to you.
-> I wanted to check in.
    <<jump check_in>>
-> Yin and Yang have been quiet lately.
    <<jump yin_yang>>
-> Can you run me through the basics again?
    <<jump controls>>
-> I'll leave you to it.
    <<stop>>
===
title: check_in
---
Instructor Tai: That's enough. The others are here — Samson, Sophia, Marcel, Hazel. All of them are doing the work. Go do yours.
-> Where should I start?
    <<jump where_to_start>>
-> I'll go find them.
    <<stop>>
===
title: where_to_start
---
Instructor Tai: Doesn't matter. Lantern Heights doesn't have a wrong door. Start with whoever pulls you first.
<<stop>>
===
title: yin_yang
---
Instructor Tai: Quiet isn't still. Listen again.
-> I'm listening.
    Instructor Tai: Good. Keep listening until you hear them both.
    <<stop>>
-> I'll pay more attention.
    <<stop>>
===
title: controls
---
Instructor Tai: Arrow keys to move. Z to jump. Shift to run. C to dash. Press F1 if you need the full list — it'll be there.
-> What about combat?
    <<jump combat>>
-> That's what I needed.
    <<stop>>
===
title: combat
---
Instructor Tai: X for melee. S to guard or parry. A switches your stance between Yin and Yang. Sparring with Samson will sharpen it faster than I can explain it.
-> I'll find Samson.
    <<stop>>
-> Anything else?
    Instructor Tai: Nothing I can tell you. The rest has to be felt.
    <<stop>>
===
